w be consumed by SAP BTP services. It’s up to the services to determine when they start using the new version.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-03\nValid as Of: 2025-09-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 164 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Configurations API - Return All Explanations for a Conflict\nDescription: Only one dependency explanation used to be returned for a conflict, even if more dependencies with maintained explanations were involved. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-27\nValid as Of: 2025-09-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 165 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Configurations API – Abort Explosion of Incorrectly Modeled BOMs\nDescription: Modeling recursive BOMs without any condition terminating the recursion used to cause stack overflow errors. This issue has been corrected by implementing early detection and returning an appropriate error message pointing to the relevant BOM positions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-27\nValid as Of: 2025-09-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 166 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Configurations API – Improved Performance for Possible Values\nDescription: Unnecessary operations used to be done when handling possible values which could cause bad performance, especially during AVC Forwarding. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-04\nValid as Of: 2025-09-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 167 ---\nComponent: Content Agent Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Credential Rotation\nDescription: Now, using Create Destination for an existing destination, the system automatically recreates credentials and overwrites the configuration, ensuring secure and consistent updates.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-03\nValid as Of: 2025-09-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 168 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: IBM MQ Adapter Supports New Version\nDescription: A new version 1.4.0 of the IBM MQ adapter supports On-Premise Connectivity via Cloud Connector for JMS Variants.  See: IBM MQ Adapter\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-03\nValid as Of: 2025-09-03\nVersion: 2506\n\n--- Record 169 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Telemetry module: Update to version 1.46.0\nDescription: The new version brings the following improvements:       We've simplified and improved the Telemetry pipeline views in Kyma dashboard (#2354).      Logs: The status of the Telemetry resource now lists the OTLP push endpoints for logs (#2336).      Logs: We've improved the security settings for the log agents (#2348).      Metrics: The MetricPipeline  runtime input now collects metrics for the default network interfaces of Nodes (#2083).      Logs, Metrics, and Traces: Update to OTel Collector 0.132.0 (#2393).      Logs: Update to Fluent Bit 4.0.7 (#2365).    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-20\nValid as Of: 2025-09-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 170 ---\nComponent:", " (#2083).      Logs, Metrics, and Traces: Update to OTel Collector 0.132.0 (#2393).      Logs: Update to Fluent Bit 4.0.7 (#2365).    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-20\nValid as Of: 2025-09-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 170 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Activity Mappings for BPMN Models > User Task Mappings\nDescription: When you import a BPMN model, a User Task is now transformed into a Form activity in SAP Build Process Automation.See User Task Mappings.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-03\nValid as Of: 2025-09-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 3301 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Custom Schemas\nDescription: You can view via the administration console the assigned attributes from custom schemas. See List and Edit User Details.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-12\nValid as Of: 2024-03-12\nVersion: 25778\n\n--- Record 3302 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: OpenID Connect\nDescription: You can configure URI for JSON web key retrieval for client authentication. See Configure JWT for OAuth Client Authentication.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-12\nValid as Of: 2024-03-12\nVersion: 25778\n\n--- Record 3303 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: OpenID Connect\nDescription: You can add authentication context class references for OpenID Connect corporate IdPs. See Configure Authentication Context (SAML 2.0).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-12\nValid as Of: 2024-03-12\nVersion: 25778\n\n--- Record 3304 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Identity Authentication has been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-12\nValid as Of: 2024-03-12\nVersion: 25778\n\n--- Record 3305 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Connectivity Proxy for Kubernetes - Kyma Integration\nDescription: As previously announced (February 26, 2024), on-premise connectivity in the Kyma environment will be handled by a Kyma module called connectivity-proxy.   This module is now available and can be activated by customers. The result is backward-compatible to the previous built-in solution, but the activation involves a short migration downtime (see previous announcement). Note  Keep in mind that all remaining users using the previous solution will be migrated centrally on March 16 within the announced maintenance window.  For more information, see On-Premise Connectivity in the Kyma Environment.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-03-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3306 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Destination Service - New Feature\nDescription: A new entity called destination fragment has been introduced. Each fragment is a key:value pair and is used to extend and override the properties of a destination at runtime.   This lets you avoid configuration duplication by keeping common properties within a destination and extracting various specific properties into dedicated fragments. At runtime the application can decide which fragment to apply to the base destination, based on the particular scenario.   You can use destination fragments through the Destination service REST API.  For more information, see Destination Fragments.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-03-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3307 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Custom IdP Users for Deployment to Cloud Foundry\nDescription: In the Acceptance and Release stages of your job, you can now use technical users from your custom identity provider for the deployment to a Cloud Foundry space.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-12\nValid as Of: 2024-03-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3308 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Extended autocompletion with function parameters\nDescription: The autocomplete functionality of the JSON transformation editor is extended to support more function parameters. For example, beginIndex and endIndex of the substring function and others.   For more information, see: Transformation Functions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-20\nValid as Of: 2024-03-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3309 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Missing AS ABAP destination error\nDescription: When exporting an AS ABAP provisioning system and importing it into an SAP Cloud Identity Services tenant, you'll get an error if no destination is available for selection. Also, you are not allowed to save the imported system without the mandatory RFC destination.  For more information, see: SAP Application Server ABAP.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-20\nValid as Of: 2024-03-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3310 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Telemetry module: Update to version 1.10.0\nDescription: The new version brings the following improvements:  Telemetry Manager:      Renamed the deployment “telemetry-operator” to “telemetry-manager” in the kyma-system", "\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-20\nValid as Of: 2024-03-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3310 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Telemetry module: Update to version 1.10.0\nDescription: The new version brings the following improvements:  Telemetry Manager:      Renamed the deployment “telemetry-operator” to “telemetry-manager” in the kyma-system namespace (#651).      Traces and Metrics:      Update to OTel Collector 0.95 (#815).      Traces and Logs:      Enriched the resource status conditions for TracePipeline and LogPipeline with the attributes “status” and “reason” to be aligned with Kubernetes conventions (#772).      Logs:      Update to FluentBit 2.2.2 (#794).    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-26\nValid as Of: 2024-03-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 1551 ---\nComponent: Cloud Portal Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP SuccessFactors\nDescription: SAP SuccessFactors has been removed from the list of supported content providers in SAP Help Portal, as it was added accidentally.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-23\nValid as Of: 2025-01-23\nVersion: 2413B\n\n--- Record 1552 ---\nComponent: Cloud Portal Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Tracking Imports in the Transport Manager \nDescription: A new screen has been added to the Site Manager – the Transport Manager.   Administrators can use the Transport Manager, accessed from the side panel, to track the progress of an import process. As a result, this process no longer takes control of the Site Manager, allowing administrators to continue working during the import. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-15\nValid as Of: 2025-01-23\nVersion: 2413B\n\n--- Record 1553 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Introduction of tags in SAP Cloud Transport Management\nDescription: You can now tag transport nodes, allowing you to group them based on the assigned tags. You can use tags to add additional information, such as project details, or system characteristics. The tags appear as labels on the Transport Nodes screen, providing more information at a glance beyond just the description field.  See:   Create Transport Nodes  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-23\nValid as Of: 2025-01-23\nVersion: 2413b\n\n--- Record 1554 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Option to download MTA operation logs directly from the Log of Transport Request\nDescription: For MTA deployment on Cloud Foundry, the log of the transport request now contains additional information about how to download the corresponding MTA operation logs, and includes a link to download the logs of the deploy operation directly from the SAP Cloud Transport Management user interface. Like this, you can obtain the MTA logs without using the Cloud Foundry command- line interface (cf cli).   See:   Options to Display Information about Transport Requests  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-23\nValid as Of: 2025-01-23\nVersion: 2413b\n\n--- Record 1555 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Option to download transport action logs in a .csv file format.\nDescription: You can now download transport action logs as .csv files, either individually or all at once. This structured format simplifies data analysis and enhances audit compliance.  See:   Transport Action Logs  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-23\nValid as Of: 2025-01-23\nVersion: 2413b\n\n--- Record 1556 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Destination Service - New Features\nDescription:   When calling the Destination service, you can now provide a previously generated and signed SAML assertion when fetching an OAuth2SAMLBearerAssertion destination. This SAML assertion will be exchanged for a token with the configured token service, instead of the Destination service generating one based on a provided user token.  A new Destinations UI for managing destination configuration objects is now available as a BETA version in the SAP BTP cockpit, side-by-side with the current UI. It is not yet at feature parity with the current UI, but feel free to try it out and send us your feedback.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-23\nValid as Of: 2025-01-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1557 ---\nComponent: Extensions\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Use a New Formation of Type Integration with Joule\nDescription: You can use Joule in SAP systems. To do that, you have to integrate these systems with Joule by including them in a formation of type Integration with Joule. The integration is between the Joule system and every SAP system in the formation, but not between each and every SAP system.  See Enabling Joule.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-23\nValid as Of: 2025-01-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1558 ---\nComponent: Extensions\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Use a New Formation of Type Integration with SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nDescription: You can configure the connectivity between an SAP S/4HANA Cloud system and an SAP Advanced Financial Closing system using the new formation type Integration with SAP Advanced Financial Closing.  See Automating Integrations with SAP Advanced Financial Closing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine o